      "exampleTransliteration": "nataqābalu fī l-maḥaṭṭati qabla an yanṭaliqa l-qiṭāri",
      "exampleEnglish": "We meet each other at the station before the train departs.",
      "grammarNote": "A closing capstone for levels 71-80: نَتَقَابَلُ ('we meet each other', Form VI, level 71) فِي الْمَحَطَّةِ ('at the station', level 68), then قَبْلَ أَنْ يَنْطَلِقَ الْقِطَارُ ('before the train departs') — a new but fully justified combination: قَبْلَ (level 67) can take either a plain genitive noun, as level 67 taught, or أَنْ + a verb (level 48's subjunctive-reuse trick), exactly like English 'before' can take either a noun ('before the train') or a clause ('before the train departs'). 80 of 100 levels now authored. مَعًا ('together') joins the -ًا adverb family and fits the reciprocal theme of this batch's meeting/departing verbs.",
      "audio": { "id": "phrase_nataqabalu_almahatta_qabla_an_yantaliq_alqitaar", "text": "نتقابل في المحطة قبل أن ينطلق القطار" },
      "introducedInLevel": 80
    }
